flowchart TD
  user["You"]
  pane["Agent pane"]
  shell["Tauri shell"]
  cli["Terminal and agent CLI"]
  loop["Loopback server"]
  target["Target pane (optional)"]
  repo["Project repo"]

  user -->|"clicks and messages"| pane
  pane -->|"Tauri commands"| shell
  pane -->|"HTTP routes"| loop
  shell -->|"spawns PTY"| cli
  shell -->|"hosts"| loop
  shell -->|"Tauri events"| pane
  cli -->|"edits, gated by hooks"| repo
  cli -->|"Worklist calls"| loop
  loop -->|"serves project content"| target
  repo -.->|"conventions it should follow"| cli

%% Hover text for boxes and arrow labels, keyed by the label exactly as drawn.
%% tip: You :: Anyone who uses Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode or Antigravity, working from the root of a git repo.
%% tip: Agent pane :: Bram's own UI, an XMLUI app in an iframe: Worklist, Transcript, Sessions and more.
%% tip: Tauri shell :: The Rust host (src-tauri/src/lib.rs): PTY, loopback server, scheme handlers, watchers.
%% tip: Terminal and agent CLI :: xterm.js in the host page, wired to a PTY running claude, codex, opencode or agy (Antigravity).
%% tip: Loopback server :: An HTTP server on 127.0.0.1 inside the Rust host; its port is in .bram-port in the state folder (resources/ unless .bram/ exists). A common gate refuses foreign Origins on state changes and Hosts that are not loopback.
%% tip: Worklist calls :: How an agent advances, prunes or commits an item. Claude, OpenCode and Antigravity use loopback curl; Codex writes intent and result files, because its sandbox refuses loopback.
%% tip: Target pane (optional) :: A display-only iframe for the project's own web UI. Off by default.
%% tip: Project repo :: The git repo Bram was started in. State lives in the state folder (resources/ unless .bram/ exists) and in refs/bram/.
%% tip: clicks and messages :: Buttons and the message box call window helpers such as toTurn.
%% tip: Tauri commands :: The pane invokes Rust commands (queue_pty_intent, record_worklist_action_authorization).
%% tip: HTTP routes :: The pane and agents read and post to /__* routes on the loopback server.
%% tip: spawns PTY :: pty_spawn opens a pseudo-terminal and runs the agent command in it.
%% tip: hosts :: The Rust host binds and serves the loopback server on a thread.
%% tip: Tauri events :: The host pushes events such as turn-state-changed; the pane refetches on them.
%% tip: edits, gated by hooks :: Agent file edits pass through bram-guard, which allows or denies them.
%% tip: serves project content :: handle_target_scheme proxies project files to the target pane at a separate origin.
%% tip: conventions it should follow :: Dashed: seeded instructions bind the agent only if it reads and obeys them.
